  "memo": "Oregon ash grows in canyons, on stream banks, and in swampy woodlands from central California north to British Columbia. In California, it occurs in the coast ranges from the San Francisco Bay region northward through the Klamath Range and in the interior through the length of the Sierra Nevada. Its leaflets are rounder and have shorter stalks than those of velvet ash, which tend to be more spearhead-shaped with short stalks.",
